{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/205129-hunter-families","id":205129,"title":"Hunter Families","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-07-22T10:53:46-07:00","id":205129,"title":"Hunter Families","content":"Hey guys!<br /> <br /> So I had something hit me today - do any of the Hunter books make mention of family lines of Hunters? I'm picturing something akin to The Winchesters of Supernatural fame - parents pass on what it is to be a hunter to their children and such. I know <i>most </i>wouldn't want to expose their children to such a life and would rather they live a normal, blind existence but I can equally see those who couldn't stand the idea of sending their children into the world blind in case something happens to them and they end up under the fangs of a vampire or something of the sort.<br /> <br /> Is this referenced or would this happen at all?<br /> <br /> Thanks,<br /> Mabs","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/128x125q90/90/w20supportergarou125.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1612-mabs","name":"Mabs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1612_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"78"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T11:29:27-07:00","id":205169,"title":"","content":"I'm pretty sure it's been referenced in various Hunter books but I can't remember specific ones until I pop them open. And yes, it most certainly would happen. I can easily think of a family of Hunters belonging to The Union, Night Watch, Bear Lodge, or any number of groups that have families all partake in hunting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T13:40:51-07:00","id":205305,"title":"","content":"<i>Glimpses of the Unknown</i> briefly details a Compact known as The Heritage House whose primary goal is to hand the Vigil down from generation to generation. Imagine several Winchester families all working together to bring their kids into what they do, and you're not far off the mark.<br /> <br /> The Lucifuge is also one big happy family of sorts; if you manifest your infernal heritage and don't join up with them to hunt evil, then you're basically considered a rogue demonic threat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T13:46:15-07:00","id":205306,"title":"","content":"For some hunter groups, lineage is an important thing:<br /> - for the Aegis Kai Doru, the higher ranks are easier to reach if your family has been involved in the conspiracy, the longer the better. And the Council of the AKD is only made of people whose family has served the group with distinction for generation.<br /> - Task Force Valkyrie, if I remember, has a bit of nepotism, but no more than the average government agency.<br /> - In the same order of idea, the Malleus Maleficarum is an arm of the catholic Church, and in the old catholic families, it was (and in some case still is) customary for only or more members of a generation to become part of the Church or at least to serve it as a lay member. This must have cons\u00e9quences on the MM.<br /> - the Lucifuge is essentially built around the idea of lineage, demonic ones. If you're in, it means one of your ancestor was involved with dark forces, one way or the other. And since there is this optional rule that the higher a hunter is ranked in the group, the greater his longevity gets (see the Chevalier Th\u00e9l\u00e8me and the Dame of Milan), you can figure that multiple g\u00e9n\u00e9rations of the same clan can simultaneously find themselves in the conspiracy.<br /> - the Knights of Saint George: Witchfinders make it clear that some members are recruited because their lineage. Moreover, the conspiracy leader is always a descendant of King Richard Lionheart (preferably a male, which puts today's group in a crisis).<br /> - and for the Ashwood Abbey, it is shown that some people get in because of family push/tradition. Same thing with the Barret Comission.<br /> That's all I can think of now. I hope it helps you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/8.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/305-kergonan","name":"Kergonan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T21:49:30-07:00","id":205647,"title":"","content":"I have nothing substantial to add, just this:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dad's on a Hunting trip. And he hasn't been home in a few days. </div> </div> </div><a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Nrr2n2653AA\" target=\"_blank\">*Cue sweet guitar riff* </a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T22:09:50-07:00","id":205677,"title":"","content":"Rolling Dice, Hunting things, The family Vigil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2266-aermas","name":"Aermas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2266_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"128"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-22T22:23:18-07:00","id":205709,"title":"","content":"(I seriously try to run <i>every</i> Hunter game like <i>Supernatural</i>)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-24T18:09:57-07:00","id":207763,"title":"","content":"Talking about Supernatural reminded me of one old show with similar theme: Poltergeist: The Legacy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/744-korusef","name":"Korusef","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"510"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-07-25T07:11:11-07:00","id":208275,"title":"","content":"That title even sounds like a WoD game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-24T20:46:37-07:00","id":265150,"title":"","content":"Mild thread necromancy, but if you're looking more specifically for blue collar, flannel wearing Hunter families Compacts and Conspiracies mentions briefly the Yeager arm of the Lucifuge in Appalachia. I've always wanted more about them and like incorporating them into my games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T11:58:14-07:00","id":265611,"title":"","content":"I've always kind of been fascinated with the idea of members of hunter families who went rouge and sided with the supernatural against their family, in part because I'm fascinated with people who are raised in cult, fundamentalist and hate group back grounds yet manage to break away. In the aborted Wod revealed campaign I had planned with my friends before they moved, there was going a, important NPC who was the son of an Ashwood abbey father and a Long Night mother (no I'm not going to explain how they wound up together, save that they were based off the parents of someone I know). The marriage ended in a nasty divorce and the NPC wound up losing faith in Christianity due to a friend's accident, while also finding his father's activities disgusting, with the result that he decided not to become a hunter. The plan I had was for him to gain an interest in shamanism as a religion and start hanging out with the local werewolves as result. The PCs, in turn were going to wind up protecting him and the pack he was friends with from both compacts while he prepared to testify against them as part of a major case the Center for Supernatural Civil Rights (a compact of anti-hunter lawyers in the planned campaign) were preparing against them. But like I said, the campaign never got off the ground.<br /> <br /> I know that there was a member of the Lucifuge who fell in love with a werewolf in one of the stories in spirit slayers, but have there been any other rouge members of hunter families in the Wod's history?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":3932,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","user":"The young man in the cafe","date":". 09-25-2014, 03:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T13:55:29-07:00","id":265722,"title":"","content":"Sounds like he would be friends with the Talbot Group, also I don't know why Ashwood Abbey would care about what a bunch of lawyers had to say about them.....they're kind of shameless","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>&quot;Do the dead dare walk the Earth before my eyes? Will the undead raise an army, fall in, and advance? Will those who would abandon God and embrace the heretical order DARE to presume to meet my gaze!? Iscariot will not allow it. <b>I</b> will not allow it.&quot;</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3889-ninjasantaclause","name":"Ninjasantaclause","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3889_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T15:34:28-07:00","id":265772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ninjasantaclause</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/205129-hunter-families?p=265722#post265722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like he would be friends with the Talbot Group, also I don't know why Ashwood Abbey would care about what a bunch of lawyers had to say about them.....they're kind of shameless</div> </div> </div> </div>Said NPC came from the head family of the Abbey in the great lakes states (meaning that they founded and ran the chapter that all the other chapters in the area were franchises of, as explained in compacts and conspiracies.) He knew and had seen enough that his testimony could have sent every abbey member across multible states to life in prison, which is why he was hiding out with a pack of werewolves in the swamps outside Savannah GA. The CfSCR convinced him to be the star witness in a case against the ashwood abbey and long night after the monsters came out, but then the pack he was friends with wound up on TV, his family (in both compacts) saw him in the background, realized what was going on and sent assassins after him and that is where the PCs would have come in had half my players not moved away.<br /> <br /> As for the Talbot group, he liked them, but he felt that those among them that were still clinging to the &quot;lycanthropy is a form of possession&quot; theory after the monsters came out were no better than the &quot;pray the gay away&quot; people his mom worked with at her church<br /> <br /> I'm recycling some of the ideas from that planned campaign in a new setting I'm writing for a novel and I imagine that a version of this story with the Wod specific elements stripped out would be a great explanation for the fall of the Van Helsing family, but I doubt I'll get another chance to run it in the Wod (There aren't that many RPG players in my town.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Despite the user name I am actually bigender.<br /> <br /> My Savannah Setting for CofD can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/959455-the-young-man-in-the-cafe-s-savannah-georgia-setting-writeup\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> <br /> My heroes as monster tamers rules for BtP can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/975230-heroes-as-monster-tamers-rules-ideas\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3932-the-young-man-in-the-cafe","name":"The young man in the cafe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3932_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1097"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-25T18:24:00-07:00","id":265842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aspel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/205129-hunter-families?p=205709#post205709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I seriously try to run <i>every</i> Hunter game like <i>Supernatural</i>)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Man,I love that show.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-28T23:41:17-07:00","id":268040,"title":"","content":"My friend thinks that the brothers on that show have sex with each other. I don't, but I have to agree that a family who hunted monsters would be very peculiar in other ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T00:31:16-07:00","id":268057,"title":"","content":"Odd sort of conclusion to come to, since the show explicitly indicate several times that Sam and Dean are 1. <i>very </i>heterosexual, and 2. pretty seriously grossed out by the idea whenever someone raises the issue.<br /> <br /> But I suspect the biggest obstacle to a Hunter family is the idea that most Hunters just don't last very long, and often supernaturals can use the family as fodder against the Hunter itself. But in the right game, sure, could work really well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T05:29:54-07:00","id":268177,"title":"","content":"I was under the impression that the compelling (but, in this troper's opinion, people who believe this: get outta town ._. ) 'Wincest' theory preceded the in-show refutations thereof, which could mean that the showrunner was simply performing damage control by making the brothers be exposed to and react that way to discussing the issue of incest. It could also mean that they simply ran afoul of a false fan theory and decided to fan the flames of hashtag Wincest by means of injecting the cultural poison some people call 'meta' so as to better court a stranger, more devoted demographic. I personally don't believe that Sam and Deans' values would permit such a betrayal of family roles, but however you slice it, the people responsible for the brothers' reactions to incest have proven themselves not above rolling around in the depressing mud of the plague pit we call fandom; a slap in the face to people like me, who believe that they should be the ones employed to conceive of, and produce, the popular tv shows but aren't. You are correct though, Allan. What a strange theory.<br /> <br /> To get back on subject, I think that hunter families would have a hard time explaining the wounds their children incur while battling fiends.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/275-leaper","name":"Leaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar275_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-29T10:47:41-07:00","id":268343,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">If you have a complaint about a post or poster flag that post for moderation. Do not make direct accusations.</span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":148,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/148-pendragon","user":"PenDragon","date":". 09-29-2014, 02:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/863-doctor-lazarus","name":"Doctor Lazarus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"35"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-03T21:55:55-07:00","id":272031,"title":"","content":"Oh, I'm well aware the showrunners were likely responding to pre-existing fan ideas, but the fact is the idea <i>has</i> been pretty canonically refuted. Now, rolling around ideas regardless can be fun and interesting, but you can't really say that's how it is.<br /> <br /> At a <i>guess</i>, I wouldn't imagine hunter families would allow children (by that I mean &lt; 12 years old or so) to actively hunt or fight, although they'd likely train them and expose them (acting as lookout or something), simply on the basis that hunters get hurt a lot, and while someone might overlook an adult doing that, assuming he's just a thug who fights a lot or whatever, children showing those same wounds gets a lot more attention, which hunters try to avoid as much as possible. Course, a married woman showing those wounds might also attract the wrong attention too. Hmm. This warrants some thought.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1mSW2-p-SwmYw5gaqnVMQ7HcRNhVedC-aA4vB6sBclGk/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for GMs</a> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1hslzrmui6ML-v7LniQUXLNyy8o52YF9g2u6usdu-Drc/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Commandments for Players</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/207-allan53","name":"Allan53","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"966"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T11:34:40-07:00","id":272421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Allan53</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/205129-hunter-families?p=272031#post272031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I'm well aware the showrunners were likely responding to pre-existing fan ideas, but the fact is the idea <i>has</i> been pretty canonically refuted. Now, rolling around ideas regardless can be fun and interesting, but you can't really say that's how it is.<br /> <br /> At a <i>guess</i>, I wouldn't imagine hunter families would allow children (by that I mean &lt; 12 years old or so) to actively hunt or fight, although they'd likely train them and expose them (acting as lookout or something), simply on the basis that hunters get hurt a lot, and while someone might overlook an adult doing that, assuming he's just a thug who fights a lot or whatever, children showing those same wounds gets a lot more attention, which hunters try to avoid as much as possible. Course, a married woman showing those wounds might also attract the wrong attention too. Hmm. This warrants some thought.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hunters do tend to be pretty unhinged. It's not a particularly healthy lifestyle or a noble calling. For what it's worth, Supernatural has touched on how fucked up it was to raise Dean and Sam to be hunters a couple of times over the years. Like the only kind of person who could do that is a crazy guy fixated on avenging his dead wife and dragging his family down into the mud.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}